[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This is called the 144p to 4K trend that I found&nbsp; on Instagram this week and I wanted to recreate it&nbsp;&nbsp; completely inside of Claude Code. In this video,&nbsp; I\'ll show you how to give Claude Code the power&nbsp;&nbsp; to generate the images, videos, sounds, edits,&nbsp; and motion graphics all together using the Gen&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Media CLI from fal and HyperFrames from Hey Gen.&nbsp; So, here\'s an overview of what we\'re going to be&nbsp;&nbsp; looking at. First is getting set up in Cloud&nbsp; Code. Then number two, we\'re going to move on&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to creating our hero image, which in this case I&nbsp; use Cream. It\'s pretty good. Third, we\'re going to&nbsp;&nbsp; generate the hero video using Seance. Fourth,&nbsp; we\'re going to I don\'t know why I\'m catching&nbsp;&nbsp; this. Fourth, we\'re going to go into the three&nbsp; variations using another video model on the Flash.&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And then we\'re going to create our menu and edit&nbsp; all of this together, including the mouse, cursor,&nbsp;&nbsp; and the menu. Again, completely in Cloud Code&nbsp; using Hey Gen Hyperframes. Let\'s get into it. So&nbsp;&nbsp; to get started, you\'re going to need Cloud Code,&nbsp; of course, and a Pro subscription. Then we\'re&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'going to get a fal account and generate an API&nbsp; key. And then we\'re going to use the fal Gen Media&nbsp;&nbsp; CLI, install that in Claude, and that\'s going&nbsp; to give Claude the ability to generate images,&nbsp;&nbsp; video, and really everything else that\'s available&nbsp; on fal. And finally, we want to make sure to add&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Hey Gen Hyperframes. This gives us an incredible&nbsp; set of tools to be able to do editing completely&nbsp;&nbsp; in Cloud Code. So step one is to generate the hero&nbsp; final image of the car. This is the 4K version&nbsp;&nbsp; of it. And I prompted to Claude once we had the&nbsp; Gen Media CLI installed to design a Falmo, which&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is a a car that\'s 70% Waymo, 30% Cybertruck, and&nbsp; to add the fal logo to the side and to make it in&nbsp;&nbsp; front of the Golden Gate Bridge in San Francisco&nbsp; at sunset. And one thing I like to do in the early&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'concept phase of a project is to test multiple&nbsp; image models at once. So I prompted Claude to&nbsp;&nbsp; generate four images from three different image&nbsp; models. We did Nano Banana Pro, GPT image 2,&nbsp;&nbsp; and the brand new Seedream V5 Pro. We also asked&nbsp; for it to generate a website that we could see and&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'we were able to see the results and compare and we&nbsp; ended up picking the one from Cream V5. I think it&nbsp;&nbsp; did an incredible design as well as making it look&nbsp; realistic and cinematic like I wanted it to. For&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'step two, we wanted to generate the sort of master&nbsp; video and we prompted for an orbiting shot around&nbsp;&nbsp; the car and we use Seedance 2.0 image to video&nbsp; again using our chosen design from Seedream V5.&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And this is the result that we got back. Looks&nbsp; amazing. And this is essentially our final beat of&nbsp;&nbsp; the video as we progress through the uh different&nbsp; resolutions. This is the 4K final version.&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Step three relies on yet another video model,&nbsp; brand new from Google Gemini Omni Flash. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp; this model does a really good job of restyling an&nbsp; existing video. So, it\'s technically a video to&nbsp;&nbsp; video workflow, and it\'s really powerful. There&nbsp; are some limitations that it can only handle&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a 10-second video, and the output is 720p, but&nbsp; the results are worth it. I tried doing this in&nbsp;&nbsp; a full C dance 2 workflow. It didn\'t turn out&nbsp; as good. So, here we are. Gemini OMNI Flash.&nbsp;&nbsp; So, we prompt to restyle only the car in Claude.&nbsp; And we say we\'re going for a 2D pixel art style,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a voxil style, and a low poly flat sort of like&nbsp; PS1 graphics era style as well. And we get the&nbsp;&nbsp; following three videos back. For step four,&nbsp; we needed to design the resolution menu. And&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I prompted for an old school gray system dropdown&nbsp; with four options: 144p, 480p, 1080, and 4K. And&nbsp;&nbsp; I also prompted for a cursor. I generated a couple&nbsp; different versions and I went with the traditional&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'gray kind of old like Windows looking system&nbsp; prompt. So finally, step five, we get to edit&nbsp;&nbsp; this all together. Again, we have our four videos&nbsp; of the same exact video but with different styles,&nbsp;&nbsp; different like resolutions. We have our menu&nbsp; and our cursor reference. And we can give all of&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'these videos to Claude Code using hyperframes and&nbsp; tell it to edit it together. And I made a pretty&nbsp;&nbsp; detailed prompt that goes through when the menu&nbsp; first shows up. It says it\'s 144p. Then the cursor&nbsp;&nbsp; comes out and changes it to the next resolution.&nbsp; And then we switch to the low poly. And then&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[04:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'we have to type out every single one of those&nbsp; steps, but once we give it those instructions,&nbsp;&nbsp; Hyperframes honestly one shot this edit. And this&nbsp; is what it looked like. So really amazing results.&nbsp;&nbsp; Hard to believe to be honest. Uh Hyperframes is&nbsp; made by Hey Genen and it\'s free. And honestly,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[04:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I\'ve been using it for generating motion graphics&nbsp; and visual effects and adding little uh highlight&nbsp;&nbsp; graphics around things. And it can even animate&nbsp; this menu. It\'s really good at animating different&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[04:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'clicks and prompt cursors. And I\'m using it for&nbsp; basically everything. But I was still really&nbsp;&nbsp; impressed that it got from just this description&nbsp; exactly what I was going for. And I really&nbsp;&nbsp; recommend checking out uh Hey Genen Hyper friends&nbsp; for free and try giving it some video footage,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[04:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'some images and telling it how you want it to&nbsp; be animated and it does a really great job. So&nbsp;&nbsp; that wraps it up for this video and hopefully it&nbsp; illustrates the power of working like agentically&nbsp;&nbsp; within cloud code to do this type of work for me.&nbsp; I\'m always asking for an HTML website artifact so&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[05:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that I can see the progress of what\'s happening.&nbsp; I want to see the script breakdown. I want to see&nbsp;&nbsp; the images and I want them like reference so I&nbsp; can be like I like number 13. And this back and&nbsp;&nbsp; forth creative process with Claude Code handling&nbsp; most of the heavy lift and the technical lift and&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[05:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'then I get to approve as the results come in is&nbsp; something that allows me to work a lot faster and&nbsp;&nbsp; I get a lot better quality in my opinion because&nbsp; Claude at this point honestly does a better job&nbsp;&nbsp; prompting than I do for the image models and&nbsp; the video models especially like Seedance 2.&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[05:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'There\'s a lot of technical things to require,&nbsp; a lot of context that you have to pull back and&nbsp;&nbsp; forth. And honestly, we don\'t need to be typing&nbsp; that stuff anymore. We can kind of highle direct&nbsp;&nbsp; what\'s happening. Also, I want to point out that,&nbsp; of course, this is a fal video on a fal YouTube&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[05:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'channel, but the fal gen media CLI allows Claude&nbsp; to use multiple image models. You can test them,&nbsp;&nbsp; pick the one you want. There\'s new ones coming out&nbsp; all the time, like Seedream just came out. Throw&nbsp;&nbsp; it in there, do a couple tests, throw it into the&nbsp; pipeline. Doesn\'t add any complexity. And then in&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[06:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this case for our example again we use C dance 2&nbsp; for the hero video which did an incredible job but&nbsp;&nbsp; I tried to do this sort of video to video swapping&nbsp; of styles with Seedance. It didn\'t do as good a&nbsp;&nbsp; job in my opinion. So we went to Gemini Omni&nbsp; Flash which is made specifically for simple&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[06:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'video to video. And we\'re just mixing and matching&nbsp; all the different models that we want. We probably&nbsp;&nbsp; could have done the audio and the sound effects&nbsp; using seed audio. And then to top it all off,&nbsp;&nbsp; we just add a little bit of hyperframes in there&nbsp; and we\'re editing the whole thing. And so we don\'t&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[06:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'have to look at this as a pure linear timeline uh&nbsp; pipeline and be done with Claude Code having this&nbsp;&nbsp; whole workflow in there. Now we can go regenerate&nbsp; a couple different images, make a different menu,&nbsp;&nbsp; and the whole process can end in the fully edited&nbsp; video again fully agentically and you can make a&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[06:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'bunch of different versions all at once. The whole&nbsp; pipeline soup to nuts. It\'s pretty crazy. Anyway,&nbsp;&nbsp; that wraps it up for this video. And let me know&nbsp; if you have any questions in the comments below.'
